-- title:
--   Scaling a modular function to a nonzero Gauss reduction
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of the local ring $A$, in the form: for every $c \in A$, $\mathrm{red}\,c = 0$ if and only if $c$ lies in `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A`. Let $f$ be a nonzero element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the subfield of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)`, itself the subfield of $\mathbb Q((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the divisor expansions of level $1 \cdot q$. The assertion is that there is a constant $c \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $c \neq 0$ such that the Laurent series underlying $c \cdot f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, that is, it can be written as a fraction $r/s$ with $r, s$ in the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` for the level $1 \cdot q$, where $s$ lies outside the kernel prime `redKer` of the coefficientwise reduction, and such that the image of this element under the induced reduction homomorphism `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom (1 * q) A.toSubring red` into $k((\mathfrak q))$ is nonzero.
--
--   This is the normalisation step making a nonzero modular function of level $q$ into a unit for the Gauss valuation attached to the component of the reduction of $X_0(q)$ through the cusp $\infty$, read through the localised reduction apparatus rather than through valuations directly. It is the first half of the two-branch normalisation at a supersingular crossing, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_twoBranchNormalisation_qpow_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_twoBranchNormalisation_qpow_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero) and [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_twoBranchNormalisation_qpow_width_dvd_and_mul_ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_eq_neg_of_eq_zero_or_eq_ofNat1728`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_twoBranchNormalisation_qpow_width_dvd_and_mul_ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_eq_neg_of_eq_zero_or_eq_ofNat1728).
